Subject: wasix: open outside the descriptor table lock, and race creates as
 open does
Last-Update: 2026-10-01

path_open opened or created the host file while holding the write lock
on the process-wide descriptor table, so the host syscall of every open
serialised every other descriptor operation on every thread, and a
server making thousands of small opens per request served requests one
at a time however many threads it ran. The host open now runs before
the lock, and the handle is installed under it, or dropped when another
thread has installed one meanwhile.

A create that lost a race to another thread answered EPERM, whether the
open was exclusive or not. An exclusive open now answers EEXIST, as it
does when the lookup finds the file, and any other opens the file the
other thread created. A lookup that found the new file on the host
before the creating open had recorded it could also leave the name with
two inodes, each insert replacing the other's. Whichever records the
name first now keeps it, and the open that created the file always
stores its host handle on it, even if another thread stored one in the
meantime, since the creator's handle is always writable.

